   "evidence": "Recovery defect: HEAD lines 362\u2013370 execute 'body = checkBody(run, pending.body, markerFor(...))' and, on failure, 'save(effect, \"done\")' before marker recovery begins at line 372. The reproduction confirms that an accepted comment is never inspected. Diagnostic defect: lines 62\u201364 log 'redactCredentials(`Issue lifecycle ${repo}#${number} run ${run.id}: ${String(error)}`)', and line 442 passes the publication exception into that logger; configured private strings are not credential-redacted. Both mechanisms already existed at base, but requirements 2 and 4 explicitly require fixed diagnostics and recovery before checkpoint closure, making these requirement gaps. The third subclaim identifies a coverage weakness rather than a runtime selector defect: HEAD's store selector already includes 'e.state IN (\\'pending\\',\\'recovering\\')', and the terminal recovery reproduction passes. The cited existing test does return the run to waiting_input before reopening, so it does not isolate terminal-run selection."
