   },
   "evidence": "issue-lifecycle.ts:362-370 runs checkBody(run, pending.body, \u2026) before the `if (pending.page)` recovery loop, and its catch does save(effect, \"done\") and continue, so no comment GET happens. Line 442 calls logFailure(run, repo, number, error), and lines 62-64 log redactCredentials(`\u2026${String(error)}`). redactCredentials only removes registered credentials, not configured private strings. Requirement 4 says to recover an uncertain prior POST by its marker before closing its checkpoint. Requirement 2 says diagnostics contain fixed codes, never exception output. Mitigations: the body is checked before every POST, so a gh error that only echoes the body can't carry withheld text, and closing without recovery never reposts. That limits the cost to the log and the record. Sub-item 3 (no test for the store's 'recovering' selector) only asks for a test."
